    <!--
      User-facing copy for the journal and the meds screens.

      One sentence is one resource. The Kotlin these replace assembled sentences
      by concatenation (`"first half " + "second half"`), which a translator
      cannot reassemble: Chinese word order is not English word order. The
      fragments are joined here instead.

      Format specifiers carry their index (`%1$s`, not `%s`) because a
      translation may reorder the arguments.

      Three things are deliberately absent. Substance names, aliases and brand
      names are data and live in the catalog's own `localized_names` table. Route
      wire values (`oral`, `insufflation`) are identifiers. And the route and
      severity *labels* shown for them are `:core:` vocabulary, so they live in
      `strings_core_vocabulary.xml` and are read through `ui.labels.CoreLabels` —
      not here, where each meds screen once kept its own copy of them.

      The `common_` names are the ones shared between the two screens: the cadence
      ladder and the small set of field labels both screens print. Everything else
      is prefixed with the area that owns it, because Android's resource namespace
      is flat and the file split only works if the names cannot collide.
    -->

